#!/bin/sh


# The guest side of the broker. A single-disc drive, period-correct: inserting a new image ejects the previous one first, then opens it in PCManFM — the autorun gesture. The host side is deliberately separate so UDisks and polkit remain outside the room.


# [[file:../../../sanctuary-redstone-9x-fvwm95.org::*Dynamic menus — recent Documents + Desktop folder][Dynamic menus — recent Documents + Desktop folder:24]]
# redstone-9x-disc — guest side of the Redstone optical-media broker.
# UDisks, loop devices, and host mounts belong to redstone-9x-disc-host.
# The room receives only the prepared host media root as a read-only rslave
# bind at /run/dotcortex/redstone-media. Never mount from inside the room.
# Verbs: insert <iso> | eject | status (mount is a compatibility alias).

MEDIA_GUEST_ROOT="/run/dotcortex/redstone-media"
DRIVES="$HOME/.local/share/redstone-9x/drives"
DRIVE="$DRIVES/D:"
DRIVE_DESKTOP="$HOME/.local/share/redstone-9x/My Computer/D:.desktop"
REDSTONE_GUEST_HOME_HOST="${REDSTONE_GUEST_HOME_HOST:-}"

host_exec() {
  # The guest home exposes the host's ~/.local/bin before the guest system
  # directories.  That can shadow the guest-compatible /usr/bin/host-spawn
  # with the host ELF, whose loader is not present in the Guix image.
  PATH="/usr/bin:/bin:${PATH:-}" \
    /usr/bin/distrobox-host-exec redstone-9x-disc-host "$@"
}

host_path() {
  case "$1" in
    /run/host/*)
      printf '%s\n' "${1#/run/host}"
      return 0
      ;;
    "$HOME"/*)
      if [ -n "$REDSTONE_GUEST_HOME_HOST" ]; then
        printf '%s%s\n' "$REDSTONE_GUEST_HOME_HOST" "${1#"$HOME"}"
        return 0
      fi
      ;;
  esac
  printf '%s\n' "$1"
}

label_of() {
  # ISO9660 PVD volume identifier: 32 bytes at offset 32808
  dd if="$1" bs=1 skip=32808 count=32 2>/dev/null | tr -cd 'A-Za-z0-9._ -' | sed 's/ *$//'
}

# Rename the My Computer drive icon to reflect the loaded disc. On mount the
# label reads "<VOLUME> (D:)"; on eject it returns to "Optical Disc (D:)".
# Edits the projected guest copy only (a plain file, reset to default on relaunch).
set_drive_name() {
  [ -f "$DRIVE_DESKTOP" ] || return 0
  sed -i "s/^Name=.*/Name=$1/" "$DRIVE_DESKTOP"
}

valid_relative() {
  case "$1" in
    ""|empty|/*|../*|*/../*|.|..) return 1 ;;
  esac
}

eject_current() {
  host_exec eject >/dev/null || {
    echo "redstone-9x-disc: host eject failed; leaving D: unchanged" >&2
    return 1
  }
  rm -f "$DRIVE"
  set_drive_name "Optical Disc (D:)"
}

insert_iso() {
  iso="$1"
  [ -f "$iso" ] || { echo "redstone-9x-disc: no such image: $iso" >&2; exit 1; }
  eject_current
  lbl="$(label_of "$iso")"
  [ -n "$lbl" ] || lbl="UNTITLED"
  host_iso="$(host_path "$iso")"
  rel="$(host_exec insert "$host_iso")" || {
    echo "redstone-9x-disc: host insert failed: $iso" >&2
    exit 1
  }
  valid_relative "$rel" || {
    echo "redstone-9x-disc: host returned an unsafe media path" >&2
    exit 1
  }
  mp="${MEDIA_GUEST_ROOT}/${rel}"
  [ -d "$mp" ] || {
    echo "redstone-9x-disc: host mount is not visible in the room: $mp" >&2
    exit 1
  }
  mkdir -p "$DRIVES"
  ln -sfn "$mp" "$DRIVE"
  set_drive_name "$lbl (D:)"
  echo "$lbl"
}

sync_status() {
  rel="$(host_exec status)" || exit 1
  if [ "$rel" = empty ]; then
    rm -f "$DRIVE"
    set_drive_name "Optical Disc (D:)"
    echo empty
    return 0
  fi
  valid_relative "$rel" || exit 1
  mp="${MEDIA_GUEST_ROOT}/${rel}"
  [ -d "$mp" ] || { echo empty; return 0; }
  mkdir -p "$DRIVES"
  ln -sfn "$mp" "$DRIVE"
  printf '%s\n' "$mp"
}

case "${1:-status}" in
  insert|mount)
    [ "$#" -eq 2 ] || { echo "usage: redstone-9x-disc insert <iso>" >&2; exit 64; }
    insert_iso "$2" || exit 1
    command -v pcmanfm >/dev/null 2>&1 && (pcmanfm -n "$DRIVE" &)
    ;;
  eject)  eject_current ;;
  status) sync_status ;;
  *) echo "usage: redstone-9x-disc [insert <iso>|eject|status]" >&2; exit 64 ;;
esac
# Dynamic menus — recent Documents + Desktop folder:24 ends here
